model mp06
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-19
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "German gift and inheritance tax: the ten-year cumulation of acquisitions from one person (§ 14 ErbStG), with the rate table and hardship relief of § 19."
  note "Each acquisition is taxed three ways, keyed by calc: total (§ 14 (1) sentence 1), fict (the earlier acquisitions under the last one's circumstances, sentence 2) and alone (the acquisition by itself, sentence 4)."
  note "No def has a time key or at, so each runs at the ask's cut, the model's on date (§4.3). C and D have no dates, so an at acq_date[q] would be a hole for them, which §4.3 doesn't define. For the dated acquisitions it would change nothing: every version read governs 2015 to 2023, and its rows haven't changed since."

source erbstrg "Erbschaftsteuerreformgesetz (ErbStRG) vom 24. Dezember 2008, BGBl. I 2008 Nr. 66 S. 3018, ausgegeben am 31. Dezember 2008: Art. 1, which restates ErbStG § 16, inserts § 14 (1) sentence 4 and amends § 14 (3) and § 19 (3), from 1 January 2009. Read in the ErbStG at gesetze-im-internet.de (zuletzt geändert durch Art. 10 G v. 22.6.2026 I Nr. 192), whose sections the locators cite, with the version histories of §§ 14, 16 and 19 at buzer.de" at "https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/erbstg_1974/"

source jstg2010 "Jahressteuergesetz 2010 (JStG 2010) vom 8. Dezember 2010, BGBl. I 2010 Nr. 62 S. 1768, ausgegeben am 13. Dezember 2010: Art. 14, which rewrites ErbStG § 16 (1) Nr. 1 from 14 December 2010. Read in the ErbStG at gesetze-im-internet.de, with the § 16 version history at buzer.de" at "https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/erbstg_1974/__16.html"

source juhn "Die 10-Jahres-Frist bei Erbschaften und Schenkungen (Nico Flegel, JUHN Partner GmbH; dated 17 November 2023, dateModified 2026-08-18)" at "https://www.juhn.com/fachwissen/erbschaftsteuer-schenkungsteuer/die-10-jahres-frist-bei-erbschaften-und-schenkungen/"

source smartsteuer "Erbschaftsteuer: Berücksichtigung früherer Erwerbe (smartsteuer Lexikon, Stand: 25. August 2025)" at "https://www.smartsteuer.de/online/lexikon/e/erbschaftsteuer-beruecksichtigung-frueherer-erwerbe/"

source wachsbg "Wachstumsbeschleunigungsgesetz vom 22. Dezember 2009, BGBl. I 2009 Nr. 81 S. 3950, ausgegeben am 30. Dezember 2009: Art. 6, which restates ErbStG § 19 (1) with its rate table from 1 January 2010 ('§ 19 Absatz 1 wird wie folgt gefasst'). Read in the ErbStG at gesetze-im-internet.de, and the amending instruction at buzer.de" at "https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/erbstg_1974/__19.html"

unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

axis mp06_total_hardship
  relieved "§ 19 (3) applies to the cumulated total, as the law reads and as Juhn's example 1.3 applies it to the same amount"
  unrelieved "the cumulated total is taxed at the plain § 19 (1) rate, as Juhn's printed working in 2.5"

index acq = [a2015, a2018, b2015, b2020, c_earlier, c_later, d_single, e2021, e2023, f2018, f2023]

index allowance_kind = [spouse, child, other_iii, unstated]

index calc = [total, fict, alone]

index chain = [ch_a, ch_b, ch_c, ch_d, ch_e, ch_f]

index tax_class = [kl1, kl2, kl3]

input acq_date[q in acq]: date

input allowance[k in allowance_kind]: money EUR

input cap_share: num

input chain_of[q in acq]: key chain
  note "The giver and recipient pair: acquisitions of one chain are from the same person to the same person."

input class_of[q in acq]: key tax_class

input hardship_high: num

input hardship_low: num

input hardship_rate_limit: num

input kind_of[q in acq]: key allowance_kind

input value[q in acq]: money EUR
  note "The value of the acquisition when it arose (§ 14 (1): the earlier acquisitions at their earlier value)."

input window_years: int

band rate_band[t in tax_class](x: money EUR): num
  note "§ 19 (1): the rate on the taxable acquisition, up to and including each Wertgrenze, by tax class. A row's lower end is the previous Wertgrenze of § 19 (3)."

def actual_tax[q in acq]: num EUR = sum(assessed[e] for e in acq where earlier[e, q]) at reader

def after_credit[q in acq]: num EUR = tax_used[q, total] - credit[q] at reader

def applied_rate[q in acq, c in calc]: num = rate_band[class_of[q]](taxable[q, c]) at reader

def assessed[q in acq]: num EUR at reader
  note "The tax actually payable on an acquisition: its due, which reads the tax on its own earlier acquisitions in turn, at the keys earlier finds (§5.10, a read at a computed key)."
  rule base = due[q]

def base_value[q in acq, c in calc]: money EUR at reader
  rule alone = value[q] when c == alone
  rule fict v erbstrg_2008 = earlier_value[q] when c == fict
  rule total v erbstrg_2008 = value[q] + earlier_value[q] when c == total

def cap_amount[q in acq]: num EUR = value[q] * cap_share at reader

def capped_extra[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR = min(extra_tax[q, c], hardship_cover[q, c]) at reader

def credit[q in acq]: num EUR at reader
  note "§ 14 (1) sentences 2-3: the fictitious tax on the earlier acquisitions, or the tax actually payable on them if higher; at most the tax on the total, as smartsteuer's Lösung 4 deducts it."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = min(max(fict_tax[q], actual_tax[q]), tax_used[q, total])

def deduction[q in acq, c in calc]: money EUR at reader
  note "§ 16 (1): the allowance of the recipient's circumstances at the last acquisition. For the fictitious tax it is limited to the allowance the earlier acquisitions used."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = allowance[kind_of[q]]
  rule fict beats base v smartsteuer_method = min(allowance[kind_of[q]], earlier_allowance_used[q]) when c == fict

def due[q in acq]: num EUR at reader
  note "§ 14 (1) sentence 4: not below the tax on the last acquisition alone; § 14 (3): not more than half of that acquisition."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = min(max(after_credit[q], tax_used[q, alone]), cap_amount[q])

def earlier[e in acq, q in acq]: bool at reader
  note "§ 14 (1): an acquisition from the same person within the ten years before the last one."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = chain_of[e] == chain_of[q] and acq_date[e] < acq_date[q] and acq_date[e] > add_years(acq_date[q], -window_years)
  rule itself beats base = false when e == q

def earlier_allowance_used[q in acq]: money EUR = sum(own_allowance[e] for e in acq where earlier[e, q]) at reader

def earlier_value[q in acq]: money EUR = sum(value[e] for e in acq where earlier[e, q]) at reader

def extra_tax[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR = tax_plain[q, c] - tax_at_limit[q, c] at reader

def fict_tax[q in acq]: num EUR = tax_used[q, fict] at reader

def hardship_cover[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR at reader
  note "§ 19 (3): the part of the amount above the previous Wertgrenze that may cover the extra tax: half at a rate up to 30 per cent, three quarters above."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = (taxable[q, c] - prev_limit[q, c]) * (if applied_rate[q, c] <= hardship_rate_limit then hardship_low else hardship_high)

def hardship_relief[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR = tax_plain[q, c] - tax_relieved[q, c] at reader

def has_earlier[q in acq]: bool = any(earlier[e, q] for e in acq) at reader

def own_allowance[q in acq]: money EUR at reader
  note "The allowance an acquisition used when it was taxed by itself."
  rule base = min(allowance[kind_of[q]], value[q])

def prev_limit[q in acq, c in calc]: money EUR at reader
  note "§ 19 (3): the Wertgrenze the taxable amount last exceeded, the lower end of its row of the rate table; 0 in the first row, which exceeds none."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = band_lo(rate_band[class_of[q]], taxable[q, c])

def tax_at_limit[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR at reader
  note "§ 19 (3): the tax that would arise if the acquisition had not exceeded the previous Wertgrenze, at the rate of the row that ends there."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = prev_limit[q, c] * rate_band[class_of[q]](prev_limit[q, c])

def tax_plain[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR = taxable[q, c] * applied_rate[q, c] at reader

def tax_relieved[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR at reader
  note "§ 19 (3): the tax at the previous Wertgrenze plus the extra tax as far as the cover reaches."
  rule base v erbstrg_2008 = tax_at_limit[q, c] + capped_extra[q, c]
  rule lowest beats base = tax_plain[q, c] when prev_limit[q, c] == 0

def tax_used[q in acq, c in calc]: num EUR at reader
  rule base = tax_relieved[q, c]
  rule plain_total beats base v juhn_method = tax_plain[q, c] when mp06_total_hardship == unrelieved and c == total and has_earlier[q]

def taxable[q in acq, c in calc]: money EUR = max(0, base_value[q, c] - deduction[q, c]) at reader

ask a_total: base_value[a2018, total] law 2026-10-19

ask b_credit: fict_tax[b2020], actual_tax[b2020], credit[b2020], after_credit[b2020] law 2026-10-19

ask b_hardship: hardship_relief[b2020, total] law 2026-10-19

ask b_minimum: tax_used[b2020, alone], due[b2020] law 2026-10-19

ask b_total: base_value[b2020, total], deduction[b2020, total], taxable[b2020, total], applied_rate[b2020, total], tax_used[b2020, total] law 2026-10-19

ask c_assessed: credit[c_later] + due[c_later] law 2026-10-19

ask c_credit: fict_tax[c_later], credit[c_later], after_credit[c_later], cap_amount[c_later], due[c_later] law 2026-10-19

ask c_total: base_value[c_later, total], deduction[c_later, total], taxable[c_later, total], applied_rate[c_later, total], tax_used[c_later, total] law 2026-10-19

ask d_hardship: taxable[d_single, alone], applied_rate[d_single, alone], tax_plain[d_single, alone], tax_at_limit[d_single, alone], extra_tax[d_single, alone], capped_extra[d_single, alone], tax_relieved[d_single, alone] law 2026-10-19

ask e_first: taxable[e2021, alone], applied_rate[e2021, alone], tax_used[e2021, alone] law 2026-10-19

ask e_increase: due[e2023] - (tax_used[e2021, alone] + tax_used[e2023, alone]) law 2026-10-19

ask e_second: base_value[e2023, total], taxable[e2023, total], applied_rate[e2023, total], tax_used[e2023, total], credit[e2023], due[e2023] law 2026-10-19

ask e_separate: tax_used[e2021, alone] + tax_used[e2023, alone] law 2026-10-19

ask f_credit: actual_tax[f2023], credit[f2023], after_credit[f2023] law 2026-10-19

ask f_fict: deduction[f2023, fict], taxable[f2023, fict], applied_rate[f2023, fict], fict_tax[f2023] law 2026-10-19

ask f_first: taxable[f2018, alone], applied_rate[f2018, alone], assessed[f2018] law 2026-10-19

ask f_minimum: taxable[f2023, alone], applied_rate[f2023, alone], tax_used[f2023, alone], due[f2023] law 2026-10-19

ask f_total: base_value[f2023, total], deduction[f2023, total], taxable[f2023, total], applied_rate[f2023, total], tax_used[f2023, total] law 2026-10-19

version erbstrg_2008
  cite erbstrg
  governs 2009-01-01..
  known 2008-12-31
  note "Known 2008-12-31, the day BGBl. I 2008 Nr. 66 was issued (ausgegeben), which carries the act of 24 December 2008 at S. 3018; it governs from 1 January 2009."
  note "Which act (§4.5), from the version histories at buzer.de (§§ 14, 16 and 19, read 2026-10-19) and the NWB editorial notes as of 22.6.2026 (datenbank.nwb.de, read 2026-10-19). This act restated § 16, so Nr. 2 and Nr. 7 have their wording from it; Nr. 1 has its wording from the JStG 2010 (jstg_2010). It inserted § 14 (1) sentence 4 and amended § 14 (3) and § 19 (3) a) and b), which no later act has changed. Which act worded § 14 (1) sentences 1 to 3 isn't established: of § 14's later amendments the JStG 2020 rewrote only Abs. 2, so this act is the latest amendment of Abs. 1, and the window row and the credit rule sit with it."
  note "Not modelled, as no row reads them: § 14 (2) as the JStG 2020 (G v. 21.12.2020) rewrote it, and the lead-in to § 16 (1) as the BeitrRLUmsG (G v. 7.12.2011) and the StUmgBG (G v. 23.6.2017) changed it. The § 19 (1) table this act set for 2009 was not fetched; the rows read are the WachsBG's (wachsbg_2009)."
  note "The rules base_value.fict, base_value.total, credit.base, deduction.base, due.base and earlier.base (§§ 14, 16) and hardship_cover.base, prev_limit.base, tax_at_limit.base and tax_relieved.base (§ 19) point at this version."
  allowance[child] = 400000 "§ 16 (1) Nr. 2: der Kinder ... in Höhe von 400 000 Euro"
  allowance[other_iii] = 20000 "§ 16 (1) Nr. 7: der übrigen Personen der Steuerklasse III in Höhe von 20 000 Euro"
  cap_share = 0.5 "§ 14 (3): nicht mehr betragen als 50 Prozent dieses Erwerbs"
  hardship_high = 0.75 "§ 19 (3) b): bei einem Steuersatz über 30 Prozent aus drei Vierteln"
  hardship_low = 0.5 "§ 19 (3) a): bei einem Steuersatz bis zu 30 Prozent aus der Hälfte"
  hardship_rate_limit = 0.3 "§ 19 (3) a): bis zu 30 Prozent"
  window_years = 10 "§ 14 (1): innerhalb von zehn Jahren"

version wachsbg_2009
  cite wachsbg
  governs 2010-01-01..
  known 2009-12-30
  note "Known 2009-12-30, the day BGBl. I 2009 Nr. 81 was issued, which carries the act of 22 December 2009 at S. 3950; it governs from 1 January 2010 (NWB editorial note to § 19, read 2026-10-19: Abs. 1 last amended by this act, in force 1.1.2010)."
  note "Art. 6 restates § 19 (1) as a whole ('§ 19 Absatz 1 wird wie folgt gefasst', buzer.de, read 2026-10-19), so the table rows of all three classes cite it (§4.5, Which act: a restatement as a whole counts), though it changed only the class II rates. The ErbStRG's own table for 2009 was not fetched, so an acquisition read at a 2009 date has no table; every acquisition here is from 2015 on, and none is in class II."
  rate_band[kl1]: [0, 75000] = 0.07 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: bis einschließlich 75 000 Euro, 7 Prozent"
  rate_band[kl1]: (75000, 300000] = 0.11 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: 300 000, 11"
  rate_band[kl1]: (300000, 600000] = 0.15 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: 600 000, 15"
  rate_band[kl1]: (600000, 6000000] = 0.19 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: 6 000 000, 19"
  rate_band[kl1]: (6000000, 13000000] = 0.23 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: 13 000 000, 23"
  rate_band[kl1]: (13000000, 26000000] = 0.27 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: 26 000 000, 27"
  rate_band[kl1]: (26000000, inf) = 0.3 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse I: über 26 000 000, 30"
  rate_band[kl2]: [0, 75000] = 0.15 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: bis einschließlich 75 000 Euro, 15 Prozent"
  rate_band[kl2]: (75000, 300000] = 0.2 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: 300 000, 20"
  rate_band[kl2]: (300000, 600000] = 0.25 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: 600 000, 25"
  rate_band[kl2]: (600000, 6000000] = 0.3 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: 6 000 000, 30"
  rate_band[kl2]: (6000000, 13000000] = 0.35 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: 13 000 000, 35"
  rate_band[kl2]: (13000000, 26000000] = 0.4 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: 26 000 000, 40"
  rate_band[kl2]: (26000000, inf) = 0.43 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse II: über 26 000 000, 43"
  rate_band[kl3]: [0, 75000] = 0.3 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: bis einschließlich 75 000 Euro, 30 Prozent"
  rate_band[kl3]: (75000, 300000] = 0.3 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: 300 000, 30"
  rate_band[kl3]: (300000, 600000] = 0.3 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: 600 000, 30"
  rate_band[kl3]: (600000, 6000000] = 0.3 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: 6 000 000, 30"
  rate_band[kl3]: (6000000, 13000000] = 0.5 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: 13 000 000, 50"
  rate_band[kl3]: (13000000, 26000000] = 0.5 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: 26 000 000, 50"
  rate_band[kl3]: (26000000, inf) = 0.5 "§ 19 (1) table, Steuerklasse III: über 26 000 000, 50"

version jstg_2010
  cite jstg2010
  governs 2010-12-14..
  known 2010-12-13
  note "Known 2010-12-13, the day BGBl. I 2010 Nr. 62 was issued, which carries the act of 8 December 2010 at S. 1768 (dejure.org, read 2026-10-19). Its Art. 14 rewrites § 16 (1) Nr. 1 with effect from 14 December 2010 (buzer.de, § 16 version history, read 2026-10-19), so it governs from then, and the spouse's row cites it (§4.5, Which act)."
  note "The ErbStRG's own Nr. 1 for 2009 and 2010 was not fetched, so a spouse's acquisition read before 14 December 2010 has no allowance row. F's 2023 gift is the only spouse's acquisition here."
  allowance[spouse] = 500000 "§ 16 (1) Nr. 1: des Ehegatten und des Lebenspartners in Höhe von 500 000 Euro"

version juhn_method
  cite juhn
  governs always
  known 2023-11-17
  note "No items: the rule tax_used.plain_total points at it, for the printed working of example 2.5."
  note "Known 2023-11-17, the date the page shows under its title (juhn.com, read 2026-10-19). Its metadata gives dateModified 2026-08-18, a record that no printed stamp beats, so the page would take it (§4.5); but the rows read are known to predate the update, so its own date applies. Wayback captures of 2023-12-03, 2024-07-25, 2025-02-08 and 2025-12-09 (read 2026-10-19) print 2.5's working as the case reads it. The update changed 1.3's printed total, not 2.5."

version smartsteuer_method
  cite smartsteuer
  governs always
  known 2025-08-25
  note "No items: the rule deduction.fict points at it, for H E 14.1 ErbStH and BFH II R 43/03 as the lexicon reports them (not fetched). Known 2025-08-25, the page's own 'Stand: 25. August 2025'."

version juhn_examples
  cite juhn
  governs always
  known 2026-10-19
  note "Examples 2.1 (A), 2.2 (B), 2.5 (C) and 1.3 (D)."
  note "Known 2026-10-19: the examples are hypothetical, so their stipulations, and the assumption that stands for D's unstated allowance, are known from the model's on date, as the model has no start (§4.5)."
  acq_date[a2015] = window(2015-01-01, 2015-12-31) "2.1 Beispiel: share portfolio in 2015"
  acq_date[a2018] = window(2018-01-01, 2018-12-31) "2.1 Beispiel: two rental properties in 2018"
  acq_date[b2015] = window(2015-01-01, 2015-12-31) "2.2 Beispiel: share portfolio in 2015"
  acq_date[b2020] = window(2020-01-01, 2020-12-31) "2.2 Beispiel: two let apartment buildings in 2020"
  allowance[unstated] = 0 assumed "the example taxes the whole EUR 6.100.000 and deducts no allowance" "1.3, Erweiterung des Beispiels"
  given assessed[b2015] = 22000 "2.2 Beispiel: Die gezahlte Steuer lag bei EUR 22.000"
  chain_of[a2015] = ch_a "2.1 Beispiel: father V to daughter T"
  chain_of[a2018] = ch_a "2.1 Beispiel: father V to daughter T"
  chain_of[b2015] = ch_b "2.2 Beispiel: father V to daughter T"
  chain_of[b2020] = ch_b "2.2 Beispiel: father V to daughter T"
  chain_of[c_earlier] = ch_c "2.5: father V to son S"
  chain_of[c_later] = ch_c "2.5: father V to son S"
  chain_of[d_single] = ch_d "1.3: A, from his father"
  class_of[a2015] = kl1 "2.1 Beispiel: daughter, Steuerklasse I"
  class_of[a2018] = kl1 "2.1 Beispiel: daughter, Steuerklasse I"
  class_of[b2015] = kl1 "2.2 Beispiel: daughter"
  class_of[b2020] = kl1 "2.2 table: Steuerklasse I"
  class_of[c_earlier] = kl1 "2.5: son"
  class_of[c_later] = kl1 "2.5: son"
  class_of[d_single] = kl1 "1.3: from his father"
  given earlier[c_earlier, c_later] = true "2.5: vor sieben Jahren; no dates are given"
  given earlier[c_later, c_earlier] = false "2.5: the later gift follows the earlier one"
  kind_of[a2015] = child "2.1 Beispiel: daughter"
  kind_of[a2018] = child "2.1 Beispiel: daughter"
  kind_of[b2015] = child "2.2 Beispiel: Freibeträge wurden in voller Höhe abgezogen"
  kind_of[b2020] = child "2.2 table: Freibetrag nach § 16 ErbStG"
  kind_of[c_earlier] = child "2.5 table: Freibetrag EUR 400.000"
  kind_of[c_later] = child "2.5 table: bereits abgezogener Freibetrag"
  kind_of[d_single] = unstated "1.3: no allowance is deducted"
  value[a2015] = 200000 "2.1 Beispiel: Es hatte einen Wert von EUR 200.000"
  value[a2018] = 1800000 "2.1 Beispiel: taxable value after the § 13d exemption"
  value[b2015] = 600000 "2.2 Beispiel: share portfolio"
  value[b2020] = 1800000 "2.2 Beispiel: two let apartment buildings"
  value[c_earlier] = 6000000 "2.5: earlier gift"
  value[c_later] = 500000 "2.5: later gift"
  value[d_single] = 6100000 "1.3: Vermögenswerte im Umfang von EUR 6.100.000"

version smartsteuer_examples
  cite smartsteuer
  governs always
  known 2026-10-19
  note "Beispiel 1 / Lösung 1 (section 1) and Beispiel 4 / Lösung 4 (section 3.2.1)."
  note "Known 2026-10-19: the examples are hypothetical, so their stipulations are known from the model's on date (§4.5)."
  acq_date[e2021] = 2021-06-29 "Beispiel 1: 29.6.2021"
  acq_date[e2023] = 2023-07-31 "Beispiel 1: 31.7.2023"
  acq_date[f2018] = 2018-12-24 "Beispiel 4: 24.12.2018 (one heading says 'Vorerwerb aus 2019')"
  acq_date[f2023] = 2023-10-31 "Beispiel 4: 31.10.2023, two months after the marriage on 31.8.2023"
  chain_of[e2021] = ch_e "Beispiel 1: father V to daughter T"
  chain_of[e2023] = ch_e "Beispiel 1: father V to daughter T"
  chain_of[f2018] = ch_f "Beispiel 4: A to B"
  chain_of[f2023] = ch_f "Beispiel 4: A to B"
  class_of[e2021] = kl1 "Beispiel 1: daughter"
  class_of[e2023] = kl1 "Beispiel 1: daughter"
  class_of[f2018] = kl3 "Lösung 4, first table: Lebensgefährtin, StKl. III"
  class_of[f2023] = kl1 "Lösung 4, second table: spouse"
  kind_of[e2021] = child "Lösung 1: § 16 Abs. 1 Nr. 2"
  kind_of[e2023] = child "Lösung 1: § 16 Abs. 1 Nr. 2"
  kind_of[f2018] = other_iii "Lösung 4: § 16 Abs. 1 Nr. 7"
  kind_of[f2023] = spouse "Lösung 4: § 16 Abs. 1 Nr. 1"
  value[e2021] = 700000 "Beispiel 1: cash"
  value[e2023] = 700000 "Beispiel 1: second cash gift"
  value[f2018] = 200000 "Beispiel 4: Bargeld"
  value[f2023] = 650000 "Beispiel 4: Bargeldschenkung aus 2023"
